From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] quick settings: Airplane mode in place of the battery tile

Plinius: while "Show Battery Percentage" is on (org.gnome.desktop.interface
show-battery-percentage) the top bar shows the percentage already and the
battery tile only repeats it, so the tile hides then; the binding follows
the key, no restart needed.

Right after it comes an "Airplane Mode" tile, in the battery's place while
that is hidden. Airplane mode leaves GNOME Settings' Wi-Fi panel, the tile
is its switch. It sets gnome-settings-daemon's AirplaneMode
(org.gnome.SettingsDaemon.Rfkill), which blocks all rfkill switches (Wi-Fi,
Bluetooth) and switches NetworkManager's WwanEnabled off; NetworkManager
then disables the modems through ModemManager, which ofono2mm turns into
oFono's Online=false. The tile is on while AirplaneMode or
HardwareAirplaneMode is, and can be tapped while gnome-settings-daemon
runs and ShouldShowAirplaneMode is set. Like the other tiles since 0080 it
says its name, the accent color says whether it is on.

New string "Airplane Mode"; translations come with the po files.
